    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The shell round builds a solid disc for two rounds and then converts the outer edge into a ruffled border by working five-"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shells"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at every other stitch. The shells fan out from the perimeter and curl slightly forward, giving the motif a three-dimensional quality that flat circles lack. It suits applique flowers, decorative cushion centres, and hat flowers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
